      "description": "Watch Blackpool vs Lincoln highlights and goals from Carabao on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 25, 2026. On August 25, 2026 , Blackpool hosted Lincoln City in a highly anticipated Carabao Cup fixture. Both sides entered the fray with high ambitions, setting the stage for a knockout clash defined by shifting momentum and tactical discipline. A Balanced Opening Act The first half saw both teams searching for an opening, but it was Lincoln City who drew first blood. In the 36th minute, Isaac Olaofe unleashed a clinical strike from outside the box to give the visitors the lead. However, Blackpool refused to go into the break trailing. In stoppage time, Leighton Clarkson stepped up to a free kick and curled a beautiful effort into the bottom left corner, leveling the score and igniting the home crowd just before the whistle. The Turning Point The complexion of the game changed entirely just seven minutes into the second half. Zac Ashworth , who had already been booked, received a second yellow card for a late challenge, leaving Blackpool with ten men. Lincoln City wasted no time in exploiting the gap. In the 53rd minute, Tom Bayliss restored the lead with a well-placed shot from distance. Before the hosts could regroup, Rob Street added a third in the 55th minute, meeting a Bayliss cross with a powerful header. Clinical Finish by Lincoln Down a man and trailing by two goals, Blackpool struggled to find a way back into the contest. Lincoln City continued to press, and their persistence paid off again in the 77th minute. Callum Elder found himself in space in the center of the box and coolly slotted the ball into the bottom right corner following a cross from Joshua Honohan . The match concluded with a 4-1 victory for Lincoln City , securing their progression to the next round of the Carabao Cup after a dominant second-half display."
